        "feedback": {
          "grade": "Correct",
          "source_grade": "Correct",
          "result": "Correct",
          "worked_solution": "We need to write and evaluate an expression representing the total number of pies.\n\nSince each of them baked $2$ cherry pies and $3$ apple pies, the number of pies each person made is:\n\n$$\n{{2}_{⏟}}_{\\text{cherry pies}}+{{3}_{⏟}}_{\\text{apple pies}}\n$$\n\nSince *each* person made this number of pies, and there are $3$ people, we must multiply the number of pies by $3.$ Therefore, the total number of pies is:\n\n$$\n{{(2+3)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{each person}}\\times {{3}_{⏟}}_{\\text{people}}\n$$\n\nTo evaluate the expression, we follow the order of operations with parentheses.\n\nFirst, we perform the operations inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2+3)\\times 3 & =(2+3)\\times 3 \\\\  & =5\\times 3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply:\n\n$$\n5\\times 3=15\n$$",
